%% L3 — Agent Runtime: agent lifecycle from CRD apply to completed run
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant GitOps as ArgoCD (GitOps)
    participant API as K8s API
    participant KC as kagent controller
    participant CRD as Agent CRD store
    participant CM as Prompt template ConfigMap
    participant TS as ToolServer CRD
    participant POD as Agent pod (orchestrator or worker)
    participant L2 as L2 (NATS / orchestrator)
    participant L4 as memory-svc (L4)
    participant L5 as mcp-sandbox-runner (L5)
    participant L7 as OTel Collector (L7)

    GitOps->>API: apply Agent CRD (system prompt ref, model, tools, memory)
    API->>KC: reconcile event
    KC->>CRD: read Agent spec
    KC->>CM: resolve prompt template
    KC->>TS: resolve ToolServer bindings
    KC->>API: create Deployment + Service + NetworkPolicy
    API->>POD: schedule pod
    POD->>POD: load system prompt, mount memory binding
    POD->>L7: span agent.ready

    L2->>POD: incoming task (HTTP or NATS subtask)
    POD->>L4: read context handle (Graphiti, Qdrant, Redis)
    POD->>L7: span run.start (gen_ai.request.model)

    loop reasoning step
        POD->>POD: LangGraph step (LLM call via Kong)
        alt tool needed
            POD->>L5: invoke tool (CubeSandbox via mcp-sandbox-runner)
            L5-->>POD: tool result
        end
        alt HITL gate triggered
            POD->>L7: span hitl.pending
            POD->>POD: pause until approval event
            Note over POD: kagent persists state; pod can be evicted and restored
        end
        POD->>L4: write episode (incremental memory write)
    end

    POD-->>L2: result (HTTP SSE or NATS publish)
    POD->>L7: span run.end (status, gen_ai.usage.input_tokens, output_tokens)
